      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): default manual TLS port to 18789 except Tailscale hosts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen Android manual gateway connect has TLS enabled and the port field is left blank, `composeGatewayManualUrl` always defaulted to port **443**. iOS only uses 443 for Tailscale `.ts.net` hosts; other TLS manual hosts default to **18789** (`GatewayConnectionController.resolveManualPort`, tested by `manualDefaultPortUses443OnlyForTailnetTLSHosts`).\n\nThat mismatch caused Android to dial the wrong port for LAN/public TLS gateways (for example `gateway.example.com` with TLS on and an empty port field).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAlign Android manual empty-port resolution with iOS `shouldForceTLS` / `resolveManualPort` rules:\n\n- `.ts.net` / `.ts.net.` suffix → default **443**\n- all other TLS manual hosts → default **18789**\n\nAlso update Connect tab port placeholder/label via `resolveManualPortPlaceholder`, which follows the same resolved endpoint as `composeGatewayManualUrl` / `parseGatewayEndpoint` (including pasted `wss://…` URLs that keep scheme default port 443).\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators connecting to a non-Tailscale TLS gateway with a blank port field now reach `:18789` like iOS instead of incorrectly trying `:443`. Tailscale MagicDNS hosts still default to 443 when the port is omitted.\n\n## Evidence\n\niOS parity source:\n\n- `apps/ios/Sources/Gateway/GatewayConnectionController.swift` (`shouldForceTLS`, `resolveManualPort`)\n- `apps/ios/Tests/GatewayConnectionSecurityTests.swift` (`manualDefaultPortUses443OnlyForTailnetTLSHosts`)\n\n### Unit tests (Windows, Play debug unit test variant)\n\n```powershell\ncd apps/android\n$env:JAVA_HOME = \"F:\\Program Files\\Android\\Android Studio\\jbr\"\n$env:ANDROID_HOME = \"F:\\Android\\Sdk\"\n.\\gradlew.bat :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests \"ai.openclaw.app.ui.GatewayConfigResolverTest\"\npnpm native:i18n:check\n```\n\nResult: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL** (full `GatewayConfigResolverTest` suite) and **`native-app-i18n: entries=2478 changed=false`**.\n\nKey placeholder/resolver cases now covered:\n\n- `composeGatewayManualUrlDefaultsPortTo18789ForNonTailnetTlsHostsWhenPortBlank`\n- `composeGatewayManualUrlDefaultsPortTo443WhenTlsAndPortBlank`\n- `composeGatewayManualUrlDefaultsPortTo443ForTailnetHostWithTrailingDotWhenPortBlank`\n- `shouldForceTlsForGatewayHost_matchesIosTailnetSuffixRules`\n- `resolveManualPortPlaceholder_matchesResolvedEndpointForBareAndCompleteUrls` (bare non-tailnet → 18789, tailnet → 443, `wss://gateway.example` → 443)\n- `resolveManualPortPlaceholder_usesExplicitPortWhenProvided`\n\n### Android emulator behavior proof\n\nEnvironment: Android Studio **Medium_Phone** AVD, `:app:installPlayDebug` on Windows.\n\nVerified on device that post-onboarding **Settings → Gateway → Connection Setup** uses the same resolver path (`resolveGatewayConnectPlan` → `composeGatewayManualUrl`). With TLS selected and an empty port:\n\n- `gateway.example.com` resolves to HTTPS `:18789` (non-tailnet TLS default)\n- `device.sample.ts.net` resolves to HTTPS `:443` (tailnet suffix default)\n\nConnect tab label/placeholder behavior is driven by `resolveManualPortPlaceholder` (same resolved endpoint as above, including complete pasted URLs).\n\nChanged files:\n\n- `apps/android/app/src/main/java/ai/openclaw/app/ui/GatewayConfigResolver.kt`\n- `apps/android/app/src/main/java/ai/openclaw/app/ui/ConnectTabScreen.kt`\n- `apps/android/app/src/test/java/ai/openclaw/app/ui/GatewayConfigResolverTest.kt`\n- `apps/.i18n/native-source.json`\n",
        "branch": "fix/android-manual-tls-default-port",
